{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"weeping-vaccinated-arrowworm","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Config-driven status mapping (map-or-drift, collapse round-trip via rebar-status labels)\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nStatus mapping is hardcoded in two parity-kept copies —\n`value_maps.py` (`LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA`) and `config.py`\n(`local_to_jira_status`/`jira_to_local_status`) — with inbound translation in\n`inbound_fields.py` (`_JIRA_TO_LOCAL_STATUS`, `_REBAR_STATUS_LABEL_TO_LOCAL`). A Jira\nproject whose workflow lacks a rebar status (e.g. no `Blocked`) currently has no\necho-safe way to remap it. Status must become config-driven on the S1 core: always\nmap-or-drift (never skip a whole ticket on status), and a non-injective collapse (two\nrebar statuses → one Jira status) must round-trip via the existing `rebar-status:`\nannotation label so inbound translation recovers the original rebar status.\n\n## Approach\n\nWire the S1 `status_map` axis to the outbound and inbound status paths. Outbound: resolve\nthe effective per-project status map (S1 `resolve_for_project`) over the built-in default\n(`LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA`); an unmapped status **drifts** (rebar keeps its status; Jira is\nleft as-is) with a recorded warning — status never skips a ticket. When a collapse maps\ndistinct rebar statuses to one Jira status, stamp the existing `rebar-status:<local>`\nlabel (same mechanism `_REBAR_STATUS_LABEL_TO_LOCAL` already consumes) so the round trip\nis lossless. Inbound: prefer the `rebar-status:` label, else invert the effective map.\nKeep the `value_maps`/`config` parity test green by sourcing both from the resolved map.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/config.py` — route status resolution through S1.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_family/value_maps.py` — built-in\n  default becomes the injected fallback.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_fields.py` — label-first inbound recovery.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_status_mapping.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\n\n- **Config-effect contrast (unit, real path):** with a `default.status_map` remapping\n  `blocked→\"To Do\"`, assert an outbound blocked ticket targets `To Do`; with no override,\n  assert it targets the built-in default — same read path, different config.\n- **Drift (failure path):** an unmapped status leaves Jira unchanged and records the\n  drift warning; asserted on the recorded alert, not a crash.\n- **Round-trip (collapse):** two rebar statuses collapsed to one Jira status each stamp\n  their `rebar-status:` label; inbound recovers each distinct rebar status via\n  `_REBAR_STATUS_LABEL_TO_LOCAL` — asserted both directions.\n- **Parity:** the existing `value_maps`↔`config` parity test stays green.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Effective status map = built-in ← `default` ← `projects.<KEY>`; a non-default\n  overlay changes the outbound target through the real path — verified by\n  `test_status_mapping.py::test_status_config_effect`.\n- [ ] An unmapped status drifts with a recorded warning and never skips the ticket —\n  verified by `test_status_mapping.py::test_unmapped_status_drifts`.\n- [ ] A collapsed status round-trips losslessly via `rebar-status:` labels — verified by\n  `test_status_mapping.py::test_status_collapse_roundtrip`.\n- [ ] The `value_maps`↔`config` parity test remains green.\n\nTest tier: **in-process unit** — outbound/inbound translation are pure functions over the\nresolved map; the oracle is the produced target field / recorded alert / recovered status.","id":"438a-e1d9-29d3-4081","parent_id":"3d7a-7795-efde-4df7","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Config-driven status mapping (map-or-drift, collapse round-trip via rebar-status labels)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787290309928978001,"uuid":"1825b379-630a-4158-8f13-ba1719acad2d"}